+/* ---------- scroll animation ----------
+   The generator wraps animated parts of a figure in .a groups: a kind (.a-*) that animates
+   FROM a start state to the drawing as it stands, and a window --s..--e on the figure's 0..100
+   clock. studio.js picks the clock by setting a class on <html>:
+   - motion-scrub (wide screens with scroll timelines): the scroll is the clock. A 1px
+     .fig-clock at the figure's centre runs it from 85% down the viewport to the middle, so a
+     figure is complete once centred; the hero, on screen at load, uses the first 500px instead.
+   - motion-play (anything else): each figure plays once over 1.4 s when a third of it shows.
+   Without a class, with reduced motion, or in print, nothing animates and nothing is hidden.
+   Fill mode is backwards so a finished animation leaves no trace on the drawing. */
